from healthcare to finance to social  media data is helping businesses  innovate to a degree that was once  deemed unimaginable but at the same time  data also presents new challenges to the  developers who are trying to make it  useful  [Music]  there are many different factors to  think about when choosing a database  especially when you're dealing with  large amounts of data  maybe you're building a music  application that aims to recommend songs  to its users based on other music that  they like  initially your app may simply recommend  the top songs to users based on the  genre they listen to the most  but what if you want to take it a step  further and provide more personalized  song recommendations using machine  learning  what if your app went viral  these situations present new challenges  to your developers  the scale of your existing database  limits what you can do because of the  massive amount of data required to power  your music personalization algorithm  where can you find a database that  scales easily allows for large numbers  of reads and writes per second at low  latency and comes in a fully managed  service  this is where cloud bigtable comes into  play  bigtable is google cloud's fully managed  horizontally scalable nosql database  that is designed to support large  analytical and operational workloads  it's optimized for applications that  require large numbers of reads and  writes per second low latency and  performance at scale  let's take a look at several of the key  advantages of bigtable  first bigtable is fast and performant  it supports large numbers of reads and  writes with the ability to support  millions of requests per second  and it's able to do so with low latency  on the order of single digit  milliseconds  one potential application for bigtable  could be collecting global air quality  data from thousands of sensors  bigtable can handle the massive right  throughput generated and also be able to  read that data quickly and reliably  bigtable is also a highly scalable  database  throughput can be adjusted dynamically  by adding or removing bigtable nodes  a node is just a set of compute  resources that provides up to 10 000  additional queries per second and is  attached to additional storage capacity  there's no downtime when you change the  number of nodes so you can seamlessly  scale up to meet the demands of a large  batch workload and scale back down once  it's complete  thanks to the scalability bigtable  allows you to store up to petabytes of  data  this can be helpful if your application  is growing rapidly and you need to scale  quickly to meet the demands of new users  bigtable is also a fully managed and  reliable database  this allows you to concentrate on  building your application rather than  spending a lot of time fine-tuning the  database  data replication across multiple google  data centers ensures high availability  and low latency for users all around the  world  in fact bigtable recently joined cloud  firestore and cloud spanner with up to  99.999 availability sla  you can replicate your data by creating  new clusters a cluster is a big table  service in a specific location  bigtable is eventually consistent so  when you write a change to one cluster  you will eventually be able to read that  change from other clusters but only  after the change is replicated  bigtable also handles backups so you can  easily recover from application level  data corruption as well as human errors  bigtable integrates easily with popular  big data tools making it easy for  development teams to get started  it is support for the open source hbase  api standard making it easy to integrate  with the apache ecosystem including  hbase beam hadoop and spark  bigtable also integrates well with other  google cloud big data products like  bigquery dataflow and dataproc  [Music]  while cloud bigtable makes sense for  many use cases there are situations  where a different google cloud database  may make more sense  spanner is preferable if you need strong  consistency globally which makes it  better for transactions  it's also a sql database which is better  for more structured data  bigquery is an enterprise data warehouse  optimized for gaining organizational  insights from large amounts of  relational structured data  bigtable on the other hand is better for  applications that need high numbers of  reads and writes per second  cloud firestore is google cloud's  serverless nosql document based database  that makes it particularly easy to  integrate with mobile and web apps  it's a good choice if you need a  flexible data model with a guarantee of  strong consistency let's learn more  about bigtable's data model  bigtable stores data in massively  scalable tables that can scale up to  billions of rows and thousands of  columns  as nosql database bigtable stores data  and key value pairs stored in rows and  columns  each row represents a single entity  while each column contains values for  each row  columns that are related to each other  can be grouped into column families for  organizational purposes  at the intersection of each row and  column combination you can have multiple  cells with each cell representing a  different version of the data at a given  timestamp  this makes bigtable great for time  series analysis  bigtable tables are sparse meaning that  if a column is not filled in for a given  row it doesn't take up any space  if you're looking for a highly scalable  reliable and fast database to handle big  data workloads bigtable may be just what  your business needs try it out for  yourself by going to cloud.google.com  bigtable and stay tuned to hear more  about bigtable
 

